# Earshot core

Earshot is a Rust library crate for Whisper speech-to-text via whisper.cpp
(`whisper-rs`), with Symphonia decoding (no FFmpeg).

## Modules

- `audio` — `AudioDecoder`, `SymphoniaDecoder`, sample-rate constants
- `engine` — `Transcriber` trait; `WhisperModel` transcription methods
- `model` — load/own `WhisperContext`
- `config` — `ModelConfig`, `TranscribeConfig`, `Device`, `ComputeType`
- `types` — `Segment`, `TranscriptionResult`
- `error` — crate `Error` / `Result`

## Constraints

- CUDA is opt-in (`features = ["cuda"]`); default CI and commands omit it.
- Do not add an FFmpeg dependency or assume it is installed.
- Prefer surgical diffs; match existing style.
- When editing Rust, follow `.agents/skills/solid-rust` and
  `.agents/skills/style-guide-rust`.
- Format with nightly rustfmt (`cargo +nightly fmt`) to honor `rustfmt.toml`.
